-- title:
--   Lift-valued cuspidal Hecke system for octahedral GL₂(𝔽₃)-extensions
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field, Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $e$ be a group isomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ onto $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/3)$ satisfying `DetDictionaryRow`: for every prime $\ell \neq 3$ and every prime ideal $Q$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ lying over $(\ell)$ with finite residue field and trivial inertia, $\det e(\mathrm{Frob}_Q) = \ell$ in $\mathbb{Z}/3$. Let $E_2, E_3, E_6$ be the fixed fields in $L$ of the subgroups $\ker(\det \circ e)$, `sylowH e` and `quatH e` (the latter the intersection of the previous two). For each of these three fields there are given real parameters $c, u, d_1, d_2$ with $d_1 < d_2$, $0 < c$, $0 < d_1$, and a finite set $T$ of adelic $\mathrm{GL}_2$-points, such that the union of the right translates by elements of $T$ of the centre-cut Siegel set with parameters $c, u, d_1, d_2$ — the set of adelic matrices whose finite component is integral of full level and whose archimedean component has, at every infinite place, local height at least $c$, squared $x$-window at most $u^2$, and determinant norm in $[d_1, d_2]$ — covers the whole adelic group modulo left multiplication by $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the field and right multiplication by central adelic scalars. The conclusion asserts the existence of a finite set $T \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ and a Hecke eigensystem $\Phi$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with coefficients in $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$ (a nonzero level ideal together with eigenvalue functions $a, b$ on the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$) such that: first, for every prime $\ell \notin T$ and every prime $Q$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ over $(\ell)$ with finite residue field, there is a matrix $M$ in the submonoid of $M_2(\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}])$ generated by the two explicit matrices `Slift` and `Tlift` whose entrywise reduction under the ring homomorphism `red` $: \mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}] \to \mathbb{Z}/3$, $\sqrt{-2} \mapsto -1$, equals the matrix $e(\mathrm{Frob}_Q)$, and with $a$ and $b$ at the height-one prime attached to $\ell$ equal to $\operatorname{tr} M$ and $\det M$ respectively; and second, both $\Phi$ and its twist by $v \mapsto \chi_{-3}(N v)$ satisfy `viaGeneralCuspNotion.IsCusp` over $\mathbb{Q}$, that is, each admits, after the embedding $\sqrt{-2} \mapsto \sqrt{2}\,i$ and central renormalisation, a continuous smooth cusp realisation at the pins `productionPinsGeneral` which has the weight-one archimedean character and is holomorphic at every real place, and has determinant eigenvalues equal to $\chi_{-3}$ of the absolute norm outside a finite set of primes.
--
--   This is the octahedral case of the Langlands–Tunnell theorem over $\mathbb{Q}$, recorded at the level of Hecke eigenvalue tables: the Frobenius trace-and-determinant table of the $\mathbb{Z}[\sqrt{-2}]$-valued lift of an octahedral $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{F}_3)$-representation with cyclotomic determinant, and that of its $\chi_{-3}$-twist, are the eigenvalue tables of weight-one cuspidal objects. It is stated here with explicit Siegel covering data at the quadratic, cubic and sextic resolvent fields, and is used by [`LanglandsTunnell.exists_liftValued_isCusp_pair_of_detDictionaryRow`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.exists_liftValued_isCusp_pair_of_detDictionaryRow), where those covering hypotheses are discharged.
